nightpanel (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * ui: emblem-ok-symbolic and preferences-system-windows-symbolic are not in
    the Adwaita theme and rendered as missing-image placeholders (tiling
    status row, preset selector, window-management category). Use
    object-select-symbolic and focus-windows-symbolic.
  * tests: every symbolic icon name in src/ is resolved against Adwaita.

 -- Greg Felice <gregfelice@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:30:00 -0400

nightpanel (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Adapter contract enforced at runtime (ADR-001). A failed command or an
    unwritable file raises instead of being logged and recorded as success;
    revert restores what was captured and refuses to guess; every file an
    adapter writes is declared, captured, and stays at its recorded path.
    A battery in tests/invariants/ applies these rules to every adapter,
    including ones added later.
  * toggle: a refused state write is recorded as a decision and exits
    non-zero, so bin/analyze-toggle-log sees the failure.
  * ui: fall back to Adwaita when the icon theme has no symbolic icons
    (hicolor rendered every panel icon blank).
  * paths: no module binds Path.home() at import; the player, the KDE
    backend and the Firefox host honour XDG_CONFIG_HOME and NP_CONFIG_DIR.
  * packaging: paths.py and runner.py are installed; they were missing from
    the install list and the .deb failed on import.
  * upgrade: tmux's snapshot shape changed. State written by an older
    version makes the first revert refuse (rule: no revert on a guess).

 -- Greg Felice <gregfelice@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:51:06 -0400

nightpanel (0.2.9-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * No functional change. The packaged payload is byte-identical to 0.2.8-1:
    all 73 files the .deb ships were verified to match, md5 for md5. This
    release re-cuts the version on a publishing path that works.
  * packaging: the publisher `bin/deploy` shells out to had been lost, which
    left 0.2.8 unpublished for six days. It has been restored, and the repo now
    refuses to overwrite a published version with different bytes or to publish
    an index that silently omits a package it could not read.
  * packaging: the three hostnames this repo named had all stopped resolving
    after the estate's rename — the apt repo, the git remote, and the ntfy
    endpoint. `bin/deploy` verified and reported a domain with no DNS.
  * packaging: the apt repo is reachable from off-LAN again. The public edge
    301'd it to HTTPS and then 502'd, so `apt install` only ever worked on the
    LAN. Both schemes now serve the repo.

 -- Greg Felice <gregfelice@gmail.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 11:24:44 -0400

nightpanel (0.2.8-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * firefox: the vertical-tabs sidebar was hidden by a `display: none` rule on
    #sidebar-main/#sidebar-box, which read as the sidebar being disabled
    outright — no keybinding could bring it back, because CSS cannot respond
    to a keypress. The rule is gone. Visibility is now Firefox's job:
    sidebar.visibility flips from always-show to hide-sidebar, so the launcher
    starts hidden each session and Ctrl+Alt+Z summons it. Under hide-sidebar
    Firefox's toggleSidebarKb handler takes the show/hide branch rather than
    the expand/collapse one, which is what makes the key a visibility toggle.
  * firefox: dropped the min-width pin on #sidebar-main. It existed to force
    the rail on screen under always-show, and it re-breaks hide-sidebar.
  * firefox: browser.startup.page, browser.ctrlTab.sortByRecentlyUsed and
    browser.sessionstore.interval move into the nightpanel-managed user.js
    block. They were the last prefs owned solely by the retired slimfox
    project, which is now uninstalled.

 -- Greg Felice <gregfelice@gmail.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 10:15:00 -0400

nightpanel (0.2.7-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * configurator: Escape now closes the window. Previously it bounced only
    between the Shortcuts and Cheat Sheet tabs (legacy cheat-sheet-overlay
    behavior) and set the stack child directly, leaving the tab-bar highlight
    out of sync with the visible page.
  * configurator: Ctrl+Tab / Ctrl+Shift+Tab cycle through the tabs in bar
    order, wrapping. All tab switches now route through the toggle group so
    the highlight always matches the visible page.
  * tests: substantial new coverage for the theming layer — tmux, firefox,
    emacs, nvim and gws adapters, expanded orchestrator state-machine tests,
    theme_service colour/brightness-clamp math, and a display-gated render
    gate for the setup-view sliders (424 tests passing).

 -- Greg Felice <greg@gregfelice.com>  Mon, 15 Jun 2026 21:59:34 -0400

nightpanel (0.2.6-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * gnome adapter: force color-shading-type=solid (and pin secondary-color to
    the canvas) on apply. Without this, a pre-existing horizontal/vertical
    shading made GNOME paint a gradient from primary-color to secondary-color
    (a black->blue gradient) instead of the solid black canvas. snapshot()/
    revert() now also capture and restore shading + secondary-color.
  * firefox bridge: new "video brightness" slider (0.1-1.0, default 1.0) that
    dims HTML5 <video> (YouTube etc.) independently of page brightness. At the
    1.0 default <video> stays untouched (filter:none, GPU overlay preserved);
    below 1.0 it dims. New video-brightness gsettings key; extension bumped to
    2.8 (keep-last-per-field commands so the two sliders don't clobber).

 -- Greg Felice <greg@gregfelice.com>  Wed, 10 Jun 2026 22:05:00 -0400

nightpanel (0.2.5-5) unstable; urgency=low

  * gnome adapter: restore the pure-black desktop background on apply (the Saab
